                {
                    "advisoryID": "OPENSSH-2024-07-01-2",
                    "severity": "",
                    "issued": "2024-07-01T00:00:00Z",
                    "updated": "1000-01-01T00:00:00Z",
                    "description": "ssh(1) in OpenSSH versions 9.5p1 to 9.7p1 (inclusive).\n\nLogic error in ObscureKeystrokeTiming option.\n\nA logic error in the implementation of the ssh(1) ObscureKeystrokeTiming option rendered the feature ineffective and additionally exposed limited keystroke timing information when terminal echo was disabled, e.g. while entering passwords to su(8) or sudo(8). This condition could be avoided for affected versions by disabling the feature using ObscureKeystrokeTiming=no.\n\nFor more information, please refer to the release notes."
                }
            ],
